🔢 Largest Element in an Array

The goal is to find the largest element present in an array.

- Initialize a variable with the first element of the array.
- Traverse through the remaining elements.
- Compare each element with the current largest element.
- If the current element is greater, update the largest element.
- After traversing the entire array, the variable contains the largest element.

Time Complexity: "O(n)"
Space Complexity: "O(1)"

## Solution

class Solution {
    public int largestElement(int[] nums) {
       int max=Integer.MIN_VALUE;
       for(int i=0;i<nums.length;i++)
       {
           if(nums[i]>max) max=nums[i];
       }
       return max;
    }
}
